Package: switchfix
Version: 0.1.0
Section: utils
Priority: optional
Architecture: amd64
Depends: libc6, libdbus-1-3
Recommends: policykit-1
Maintainer: SwitchFix contributors <switchfix@localhost>
Homepage: https://github.com/switchfix/switchfix
Description: Fix text typed in the wrong keyboard layout (EN↔RU)
 SwitchFix is a KDE Plasma tray utility in the spirit of Punto Switcher /
 Keyboop. It converts text typed in the wrong keyboard layout, switches the
 system layout, and can fix a selected sentence via an external LLM API.
 .
 Features:
  * Convert selection (Ctrl+Alt+R) via clipboard-marker protocol
  * LLM-fix selection (Alt+R): send selected text to an OpenAI-compatible
    API and replace it; one Backspace undoes the replacement
  * Auto terminal mode (clear line + Ctrl+Shift+V) in konsole/kitty/…
  * Toggle on/off (Ctrl+Alt+T) and tray menu
  * System layout switch through org.kde.KeyboardLayouts
 .
 Privacy: no keylogging persistence. The keystroke buffer is RAM-only and
 optional. When LLM-fix is enabled, only the selected text is sent to the
 API endpoint you configure. Membership in group 'input' is required for
 global hotkeys and uinput injection.
